# Internal working files — never part of the deployed site.
#
# CLAUDE.md was served publicly at /CLAUDE.md (HTTP 200, 33 KB). It exposed an unannounced
# commercial decision with its reasoning, and pointed at where the admin credentials live.
# Nothing linked from the site lives in here — only whitepaper.pdf at root is referenced,
# and *.md does not match it.
CLAUDE.md
*.md
docs/
scripts/
contracts/
build/
.claude/

# ⛔ THE FORGE IS THE ARTIST'S CONSOLE AND IS NOT PART OF THE PUBLIC SITE.
# Artist, 2026-08-06: *"no one should have access to the plate proof console except me."*
# `cards/proof.html` is the plate-proof editor the hundred are made on — every press dial, the
# save/number panel and the deck's JSON export. Unlinking it would have been obscurity: the
# pre-launch veil has been OFF since 2026-08-05 (gate.js `LIVE = true`), so anyone who typed the
# URL, or read it out of the repo, had the whole console. Not shipping the file is the lock.
#
# ⚑ IT STAYS IN GIT, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF DOING IT HERE RATHER THAN DELETING. The file is
#   still on disk, so `npm run test:forge`, `test:deck`, `test:hero` and `npm run deck:bake` all
#   keep driving it locally and the artist keeps working in it via `npm run forge`. Only the CDN
#   never sees it.
# ⚠ `scripts/test-name-law.mjs` mirrors this file by DIRECTORY (`SKIP_DIR`), so proof.html is
#   still swept for the name law. Deliberate: it is a surface the artist reads every day, and a
#   file that does not ship can still be wrong in front of the person who owns it.
cards/proof.html

# Card-separation BUILD OUTPUT — 23 MB of the 31 MB in models/cards/ that nothing fetches.
# The only thing the site reads is models/cards/<n>/layers/*.png, named by the sidecars in
# cards/art/hero/*.layers.json — resolved all 34 srcs, every one lives under layers/.
# Everything below is what png23d/Blender emitted on the way there: the packed mesh, the
# contact sheets, and card 44's source maps. Kept in git (they are how a card is re-cut);
# kept off the CDN (a collector opening one card would otherwise pay for six cards of
# exploded-view PNGs they never see).
models/cards/*/preview/
models/cards/*/layers.glb
models/cards/*/channels.glb
models/cards/*/channels/
models/cards/44/albedo.png
models/cards/44/normal.png
models/cards/44/height.png
models/cards/44/ao.png
models/cards/alley-trio/*.glb

# ⛔ THE THREE DEPLOY CONSOLES — same argument as cards/proof.html above: NOT SHIPPING THE FILE IS
# THE LOCK. All three contracts landed on mainnet 2026-08-06 and these pages have no further use.
#
# ⚑ The exposure was small but real and NOT the one that looks obvious. Nobody could wire anything
# — setRenderContract and setEdition are owner-gated and revert for a stranger. But deploy-lens.html
# handed any visitor a one-click deploy of a contract whose name is `ripmaster3030studios` and whose
# symbol is `3030L`: a counterfeit lens, at their own gas. They can still do it by copying bytecode
# off-chain, but we should not ship the button.
#
# ⚠ They were public all evening because the pre-launch veil came off on 2026-08-05 and I kept
# telling the artist to "enter the admin password" — a page I had never actually loaded myself.
deploy-render.html
deploy-sink.html
deploy-lens.html
